  "claim": "The Czech star of \"The Green Carriage\" played in \"Hamlet\". His character was summoned by King Claudius to distract the prince from his apparent madness.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Igor Dmitriev. Sentence: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev (Russian: И́горь Бори́сович Дми́триев ) (May 29, 1927 – January 26, 2008) was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions (e.g., Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\").\nPage: Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. Sentence: They are childhood friends of Hamlet, summoned by King Claudius to distract the prince from his apparent madness and if possible to ascertain the cause of it.\nPage: The Green Carriage. Sentence: The Green Carriage (Russian: Зелёная карета , \"Zelyonaya kareta \" ) is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov and Igor Dmitriev.",
