        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "934666d4-be0b-5784-8291-3959d1199161",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Dmitriev, Grigori Kozintsev, Yan Frid, Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov\n- Works: Hamlet, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern, The Green Carriage\n- Roles: Rosencrantz, Guildenstern\n- Topics: Russian film and theater acting, Soviet historical drama films\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev was born on May 29, 1927, and died on January 26, 2008.\n- Igor Dmitriev was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in portraying aristocratic characters in costume productions.\n- Igor Dmitriev played Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are childhood friends of Hamlet.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are summoned by King Claudius to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and, if possible, discover its cause.\n- The Green Carriage is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid.\n- The Green Carriage stars Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, and Igor Dmitriev.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
